sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant MobileApp as Bank Native App
    participant Backend as DES SAML Bridge (Pseudo-IdP)
    participant OOOO as OOOO (CIAM)
    box "Embedded WebView Context" #f0f7ff
    participant WebView as WebView Browser
    participant MarstoneApp as Marstone App (Service Provider)
    end
    participant Auth0 as Marstone Auth0 Tenant

    note over User, Backend: Prerequisites: User has valid Access Token from OOOO

    User->>MobileApp: Taps "Open Marstone"

    rect rgb(240, 240, 240)
    note right of MobileApp: Phase 1: The SAML Bridge (Bootstrapping Session)
    MobileApp->>Backend: Request Launch Bridge (sends OOOO Access Token)
    
    %% NEW STEP: OOOO VALIDATION
    Backend->>OOOO: API Call: /introspect (Validate Token)
    OOOO-->>Backend: Token Active (User: "john.doe@email.com")
    
    note right of Backend: 1. Token Validated by OOOO<br/>2. Backend generates SAML Response<br/>3. Sign with Bank Private Key
    Backend-->>MobileApp: Return HTML "Auto-Submit" Form (w/ SAMLResponse)
    MobileApp->>WebView: Load HTML Form
    WebView->>Auth0: POST /login/callback?connection=Bank-Bridge<br/>(SAMLResponse)
    
    note left of Auth0: 1. Auth0 validates Bank Signature<br/>2. Creates Auth0 Session
    Auth0-->>WebView: 302 Redirect to Marstone App
    end

    rect rgb(230, 255, 230)
    note right of MobileApp: Phase 2: Standard Marstone OIDC Flow
    WebView->>MarstoneApp: Load Application URL
    MarstoneApp->>Auth0: OIDC GET /authorizeRequest
    note left of Auth0: Auth0 sees active session.<br/>Skips Login.
    Auth0-->>MarstoneApp: Redirect w/ Auth Code
    MarstoneApp->>Auth0: POST /oauth/token
    
    %% OPTIONAL: AUTH0 CAN VALIDATE WITH OOOO AGAIN IF FEDERATED
    %% BUT TYPICALLY STOPS HERE FOR BRIDGE FLOW
    
    Auth0-->>MarstoneApp: Return ID Token & Access Token
    end

    MarstoneApp->>WebView: Render Dashboard
